id: pmc-help-parser
title: Document exactly the flags accepted by every standalone command
description: "Review finding from PR #278: the root help assigns contracts continuation flags to upgrades. Audit all standalone commands, aliases and command summaries against the actual parsers."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T06:47:00.485Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T06:53:21.769Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Every standalone command help and root command synopsis matches its parser in both directions, including aliases and short flags; Regression executes advertised flags and discovers parser flags independently; reverting only help fixes fails; Targeted tests, typecheck and available lint pass locally; npm and Bun release gates pass in CI"
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T06:47:04.208Z",codex-agent,"Plan: independently inventory parser flag spellings, compare command-scoped help in both directions, and execute each spelling through the real parser. Cover root, audit, contracts and upgrades, including root command summaries. Preserve parser behavior; repair all discovered help mismatches and prove failure with only help fixes reverted."
  "2026-10-26T06:49:11.421Z",codex-agent,"Inventory found root/audit omissions: -h, --help, --set-output, --statuses, --exclude-tags and --no-links. Contracts/upgrades help omitted -h and --help. Root contracts synopsis omitted --pm-root, --json and its grouping/release continuation; upgrades inherited unsupported --group-by, --section-by and --release-version. Reassigned continuation lines and documented all spellings. Current upgrades parser does accept --audience. Added an explicit audit synopsis; replaced an embedded external pm list flag with plain whole-tracker wording to keep option extraction command-scoped. No parser behavior changed. The repository has no lint script; its documented static gates are typecheck and docstring."
  "2026-10-26T06:51:20.931Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: kept test/help-parser-contract.test.ts unchanged, restored only the three modified help functions to their origin/main behavior (the only source changes), then ran node --test test/help-parser-contract.test.ts directly against src. Exit 1: 7 tests, 1 pass, 6 failures, including both root synopsis cases and all four command help cases. Restored the fixes: exit 0, 7/7 passed, no skipped tests. The linked regression also passed through pm test pmc-help-parser --run --progress. Static checks passed: npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; npm run docstring (26 files, 201 documented declarations); git diff --check. No standalone lint script is defined."
  "2026-10-26T06:53:21.769Z",codex-agent,"Targeted integration command passed: node --test test/help-parser-contract.test.ts test/cli-regression.test.ts test/audience-contracts.test.ts test/consumer-upgrades.test.ts (43/43, zero skips; includes actual non-git tracker, standalone/host/SDK agreement and 500 model operation sequences). That run started before the two independent synopsis tests were added; the final expanded help contract subsequently passed 7/7, including via pm test. Changelog generation and link validation passed. Local pm health reports the unchanged legacy provenance baseline plus a clone-local managed pm-github host-version skew; clean CI health remains the acceptance gate. Preparing the ready-for-review PR; full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI."
